cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If pydecomp helped your analysis or research, please cite it as below."
title: "pydecomp: static Python deobfuscator"
abstract: >-
  pydecomp recovers readable source from packed, encoded, mangled or
  partly-compiled Python files without executing them. It models the bytecode
  directly: its own marshal reader, per-version opcode tables for CPython 3.9
  through 3.14, an expression evaluator with a whitelist, and a polishing pass
  that demangles identifiers and removes dead branches. Every recovery is
  compiled, audited for unbound names and reported, so an output that cannot
  run is never presented as a success.
type: software
license: MIT
